{"name":"Aragon Green","hex":"#47ba87","fetched":"2026-11-01","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aragon","blocks":[{"text":"Aragon is an autonomous community in Spain, coextensive with the medieval Kingdom of Aragon. In northeastern Spain, the Aragonese autonomous community comprises three provinces : Huesca, Zaragoza, and Teruel. Its capital is Zaragoza. The current Statute of Autonomy declares Aragon a historic nationality of Spain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flag_of_Aragon.svg/330px-Flag_of_Aragon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aragon","wikidata":"Q4040"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Murallaromanadezaragoza.JPG/500px-Murallaromanadezaragoza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Murallaromanadezaragoza.JPG/1280px-Murallaromanadezaragoza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Murallaromanadezaragoza.JPG/500px-Murallaromanadezaragoza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The remains of the Roman walls of Zaragoza","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMurallaromanadezaragoza.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/WLM14ES_-_Zaragoza_Exposici%C3%B3n_sobre_Augusto_00006_-_.jpg/500px-WLM14ES_-_Zaragoza_Exposici%C3%B3n_sobre_Augusto_00006_-_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/WLM14ES_-_Zaragoza_Exposici%C3%B3n_sobre_Augusto_00006_-_.jpg/500px-WLM14ES_-_Zaragoza_Exposici%C3%B3n_sobre_Augusto_00006_-_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bust of Augustus found in Tarazona","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWLM14ES_-_Zaragoza_Exposici%C3%B3n_sobre_Augusto_00006_-_.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Syd_1358.jpg/330px-Syd_1358.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Syd_1358.jpg/330px-Syd_1